# The Claude Code sandbox blocks outbound port 22 but allows localhost, so
# agent sessions can't SSH directly to any real host. com.technicalpickles.
# agent-ssh-relay (a LaunchAgent running gost, an unsandboxed SOCKS5 proxy,
# on 127.0.0.1:1080) relays connections through, restricted to an explicit
# host:port allowlist in config/gost/agent-ssh-relay.yml. This ProxyCommand
# applies to every destination in an agent session -- the allowlist, not
# this file, decides what's actually reachable. Add a git host by editing
# the YAML, not by adding another Match block here.
Match exec "test -n \"$CLAUDECODE\""
  ProxyCommand ncat --proxy 127.0.0.1:1080 --proxy-type socks5 %h %p
